# Engineering standards

These standards apply to all work in this repository. They are enforced by hooks
where possible and by review everywhere else.

## Architecture
- All reusable logic lives in the **service layer**. Do not inline domain logic in
  controllers, route handlers, or UI components.
- Before writing a new function, search for an existing one to reuse. Prefer extending
  a service over duplicating logic.
- Keep domains isolated: no cross-domain database access; communicate across bounded
  contexts via explicit APIs or events, not shared tables.
- Wrap external systems in an anti-corruption layer (adapter); never let a third-party
  model leak into domain code.

## Pull requests
- Keep PRs under ~1,000 lines. If a change is larger, stop and propose a stacked-PR
  split before writing code.
- One feature concern per PR. Each stacked PR must build cleanly on the previous branch.

## Testing
- Tests are the definition of done. A change isn't complete until the suite is green.
- Expand test coverage for the edge cases raised in review rather than only the happy path.

## Security
- **Never install a dependency published less than 14 days ago.** (Enforced by the
  `dep-age-guard` hook.)
- Prefer hardware/app-based 2FA over SMS for any account an agent can reach.

## Context discipline
- Start a fresh thread per feature. When context grows heavy (~70%), run `/handoff`
  to persist state, then clear.
- Plans live as markdown in `plan/` — they are for you as much as for the agent.
